Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: omit undecoded HEVC references from native DPB

A CRA entered after flush can retain unavailable pre-access pictures as
software DPB placeholders. They have no submitted capture timestamp and
cannot identify a native reference surface. Omit them from the exported
DPB; an actually used missing reference still resolves to index 0xff and
is rejected by native control validation rather than fabricated.

--- a/libavcodec/v4l2_req_hevc_vx.c
+++ b/libavcodec/v4l2_req_hevc_vx.c
@@ -333,9 +333,14 @@ fill_dpb_entries(const HEVCContext * const h, struct v4l2_hevc_dpb_entry * const entries)
     for (i = 0; i < FF_ARRAY_ELEMS(h->DPB); i++) {
         const HEVCFrame * const frame = &h->DPB[i];
         if (frame != pic && (frame->flags & (HEVC_FRAME_FLAG_LONG_REF | HEVC_FRAME_FLAG_SHORT_REF))) {
+            const uint64_t timestamp = frame_capture_dpb(frame->frame);
+            /* Missing pre-CRA pictures have no submitted native surface. */
+            if (!timestamp)
+                continue;
+
             struct v4l2_hevc_dpb_entry * const entry = entries + n++;
 
-            entry->timestamp = frame_capture_dpb(frame->frame);
+            entry->timestamp = timestamp;
 #if HEVC_CTRLS_VERSION <= 2
             entry->rps = find_frame_rps_type(h, entry->timestamp);
 #else
